---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
const mailto = `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Project inquiry')}`;
---
<Base title="Software, AI systems, and physical parts" description={site.tagline}>
  <section class="section band-dark">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">{site.legalName} · {site.location}</p>
      <h1>I build the thing you can't buy off the shelf.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Software, AI systems, and 3D-printed parts from a one-person studio in Louisville. I'm JT Embry, owner of Embry Development, LLC, with a decade of fintech and healthtech engineering behind every job.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={mailto}>Start a conversation</a> <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/services">See what I build</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid">
      <div><span class="stat">10+ yrs</span>building fintech and healthtech products</div>
      <div><span class="stat">65%</span>more tickets shipped per sprint after I set a team's AI tooling direction</div>
      <div><span class="stat">Every service</span>on a production platform moved to a new cloud, end to end</div>
      <div><span class="stat">1 month</span>from first ask to a live site a small-business owner runs herself</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Four things I build</h2>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>AI adoption for engineering teams</h3>
          <p class="problem">"We bought the AI seats and nothing changed."</p>
          <p>A four-week pilot on one real repo: audit the workflow, set up agents where they pay off, measure before and after. <a href="/services#teams">How it works</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Knowledge assistants for small practices</h3>
          <p class="problem">"Our knowledge is in documents nobody can search."</p>
          <p>A private assistant over your own files, on infrastructure you control, that answers with citations. <a href="/services#practices">How it works</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Websites and automation for small businesses</h3>
          <p class="problem">"We need a site and the plumbing behind it without an agency bill."</p>
          <p>A fast site you own on your own domain, hosted for free, plus the forms, booking, and email behind it. <a href="/services#small-business">How it works</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Design and 3D printing</h3>
          <p class="problem">"We need a part, a prototype, or a small run that no catalog sells."</p>
          <p>CAD from your sketch or measurements, functional prints, small batches. You get the part and the files. <a href="/printing">How it works</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>How working with me goes</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><strong>Tell me the problem.</strong> One email is enough. I'll say honestly whether it's something I should build.</li>
        <li><strong>One-page scope.</strong> What you get, what it costs, and when. Fixed price wherever the work can be scoped.</li>
        <li><strong>Build in the open.</strong> Something working you can see every week, not a reveal at the end.</li>
        <li><strong>Hand over.</strong> You own the code, the files, and the parts. No lock-in.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={mailto}>Start a conversation</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
